            <title>[LU-21158] sanity-sec test_27e: NULL pointer dereference in gss_sec_display_kr reading osc srpc_contexts</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21158</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity-sec test_27e: client (el8.10, 4.18.0-553) oopses with a NULL pointer dereference in gss_sec_display_kr() while lctl reads osc.*.srpc_contexts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Crash log (sanity-sec.kernel-crash.trevis-154vm124.log):&lt;br/&gt;
  BUG: unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at 0000000000000000&lt;br/&gt;
  RIP: gss_sec_display_kr+0xc8/0x300 &lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;ptlrpc_gss&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
  Call Trace: sptlrpc_ctxs_lprocfs_seq_show+0x63 &lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;ptlrpc&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;, seq_read, full_proxy_read, vfs_read&lt;br/&gt;
  Comm: lctl, on "lctl get_param &lt;del&gt;n osc.&lt;b&gt;OST&lt;/b&gt;-osc&lt;/del&gt;&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;^M&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;^D&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;^T&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;*.srpc_contexts"&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Just before: the client remounted with skpath=.../nodemap/c0.key on a fileset (d27e.sanity-sec/prim/s) and logged "ll_force_readonly(): mount failed due to read-only fileset, forcing read-only mount: rc = -30"; the test then reads srpc_info and srpc_contexts on mdc and osc, and the osc read crashed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;gss_sec_display_kr() walks sec-&amp;gt;gsk_clist under ps_lock and dereferences per context state (key, peer connection) without checking each pointer; sptlrpc_ctxs_lprocfs_seq_show() only takes a reference on the import's sec. Related older crashes in the same lprocfs path: &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-10451" title="sptlrpc_ctxs_lprocfs_seq_show crash in recovery-small test 57" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-10451"&gt;LU-10451&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18689" title="recovery-small test 57 crashes in osp and sptlrpc" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18689"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18689&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (recovery-small test 57).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not caused by the patch under test: change 67691 (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20553" title="MDD: DoM not detected on SEL (DoM + extension) layouts" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20553"&gt;LU-20553&lt;/a&gt;) only changes mdd_lmm_dom_size() in the MDD layer. The crash is on the client in ptlrpc_gss. One failure in 870 review runs of review-dne-selinux-ssk-part-2 in the 30 days before; no earlier sanity-sec test_27e crash with this signature (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20700" title="sanity-sec test_27e: crashed during sanity-sec test_27e" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20700"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20700&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is a different crash, lmv_disconnect_mdc use after free, fixed by change 68875).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Session: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/7c036284-369f-48f7-8c23-1d347f8e07b6" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/7c036284-369f-48f7-8c23-1d347f8e07b6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-67691-ps5-a54365d95cf1 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/67691" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/67691&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
